      ],
      "status": "affected",
      "action_statement": "Update nodejs-24 to 24.22.1-r0 or later.",
      "status_notes": "CVE-2026-105483: tls.checkServerIdentity() does not treat an IPv4 host written with non-ASCII digits, such as fullwidth digits, as an IP address and matches it against certificate DNS names, so a certificate without a matching IP SAN can authenticate the connection. Node.js fixed it on the 24.x line in 24.22.1, the October 2026 security release (https://nodejs.org/en/blog/vulnerability/october-2026-security-releases, https://github.com/nodejs/node/releases/tag/v24.22.1), with https://github.com/nodejs/node/commit/de49c913f2 (tls: fix ip normalization regression). We read the version string from the node binary in every published nodejs-24 package for Alpine 3.23 in the DHI Alpine repository (24.13.0-r0 to the current 24.22.3-r0, x86_64 and aarch64); each matches its package version, so builds below 24.22.1-r0 ship Node.js 24.22.0 or older and 24.22.1-r0 and every later build ship 24.22.1 or newer. The range ends at 24.22.1-r0, the first fixed build."
    },
